    skos:definition """Natural environments and wildlife is the study of the relationships between living organisms in natural environments in order to protect nature and wildlife. It includes the study of establishing and maintaining national parks in order to preserve their original natural state.
Programmes and qualifications with the following main content are classified here:
National parks and wildlife management
Nature conservation
Wildlife

=== Exclusions
Study of agriculture, horticulture and forestry are excluded from this detailed field and included in some of the detailed fields under 08 'Agriculture, forestry, fisheries and veterinary'.
Study of hunting and trapping is excluded from this detailed field and included in detailed field 0821 'Forestry'."""@fr ;
