    skos:definition """Electronics and automation is the study of planning, designing, developing maintaining and monitoring electronic equipment, machinery and systems. It includes designing computers and equipment for communication.
Programmes and qualifications with the following main content are classified here:
Broadcasting electronics
Communication systems
Communications equipment installation
Communications equipment maintenance
Computer engineering
Computer repairing
Control engineering
Data processing technology
Digital technology
Electronic engineering
Electronic equipment servicing
Network technology
Robotics
Telecommunications technology
Television and radio repairing

=== Exclusions
Computer science (Software and applications development) is excluded from this detailed field and included under 0613 'Software and applications development and analysis'."""@fr ;
