    skos:definition """Child care and youth services are the study of the development and non-medical care of children and youths. It includes the study of recreation and leisure activities as a social service for school children and young adults.
Programmes and qualifications with the following main content are classified here:
Child care
Child recreation programmes
Day care
Non-medical care of disabled children
Youth services
Youth worker programmes

=== Exclusions
Study of early childhood education in pre-schools is excluded from this detailed field and included in detailed field 0112 'Training for pre-school teachers'.
Study of health care of children is excluded from this detailed field and included in detailed field 0913 'Nursing and midwifery'."""@fr ;
